# Documentation

Follow [human-ai-docs](human-ai-docs.mdc) for the README vs AGENTS.md boundary. For product “why / ambition / comparison,” read [AGENTS.md → Product intent](../../AGENTS.md) before rewriting marketing prose.

## Human README contract

When creating or editing any `README.md` **except** `docs/README.md`:

1. **Overview & pitch** — what it is, why it matters (outcome language; see Product intent).
2. **Why use it** (root / major packages) — short value bullets.
3. **Quick start** — prerequisites + one minimal install/usage example.
4. **Features that matter** — capabilities users feel; not stack trees as the hero.
5. **Packages / links** — point to sibling READMEs or `docs/` for depth.
6. **Contributing & license** — brief; no agent prompts or Cursor rules in README body.

Discover facts from that package’s manifest (`Cargo.toml`, `.csproj`, `dhara.config.toml`), code, and workflows. Use **reference-style** markdown links. Prefer linking `docs/` over duplicating ABI, pipeline, or architecture essays.

## Publish and discovery surfaces

| README | Audience / surface |
|--------|-------------------|
| [`README.md`][root-readme] | **GitHub** — product pitch, dual quick start, package map |
| [`src/core/dhara_storage/README.md`][crate-dhara-storage] | **crates.io** |
| [`src/core/dhara_storage_dal/README.md`][crate-dal] | **crates.io** |
| [`src/bindings/dharastorage-ffi/README.md`][crate-dharastorage] | Native ABI (workspace; NuGet asset) |
| [`src/bindings/csharp/Dhara.Storage/README.md`][nuget-readme] | **NuGet** |
| [`tooling/drot/README.md`][crate-tool] | **DROT submodule** (operator CLI; not crates.io) |
| Folder READMEs under `src/`, `tooling/` | **GitHub folder discovery** — short blurbs only |

Scope package READMEs to that package. Root README: pitch + how to try it + where packages live — not CI/operator essays.

**Exception:** `tooling/drot/src/drot_dhara_storage/package/README.md` is internal operator notes — keep short; not the human publish layout.

## `docs/**` (including `docs/README.md`)

- Filename: `docs/<topic>.md` (kebab-case); optional assets under `docs/references/`.
- Update [docs/README.md][docs-index] when adding a top-level doc.
- Tone: implementer/operator reference — not product marketing.

## Must not

- Put agent prompts, Cursor rules, or skill instructions in any README.
- Assume only the repo-root README exists or matters.
- Paste design lineage or stack-first delivery stories that Product intent says to omit from READMEs.

